// base32, RFC 4648 §6: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4648#section-6
// base32hex, RFC 4648 §7: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4648#section-7
//
// Five bits a character, padded to eight characters a group. The extended-hex
// alphabet keeps byte order, which is why a sorted list of encodings is a
// sorted list of payloads.
//
// Crockford's base32 (https://www.crockford.com/base32.html) and z-base-32
// (https://philzimmermann.com/docs/human-oriented-base-32-encoding.txt) are the
// same five bits for a different reader: one drops the letters a human confuses
// with digits, the other orders its alphabet by how often a letter is used.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonbase",
  "moonbitstack/moonbase/internal",
}
